  "memory_update": "For this teacher (5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top1, teacher_pic50 7.8378, anchor ticks [5,5,5,5]): recorded direction to avoid repeating - nominal amplitude changes near the current scale are nearly inert because effective guidance displacement is ~1e-3 A and no clipping occurs, so further small tweaks that do not raise inside_rms_A out of the 1e-3 A regime should be treated as low-information. The 0.42 win rate and per-quartile ~1e-4 deficits say the last round is a tie, not a genuine degradation, so the incumbent is retained as the shared parent. Open questions for the next evidence request: does raising interval 0 alone (10-25) produce the largest inside_rms_A gain and does that gain map to Q3/Q4 rescored pIC50; does weakening the late interval (76-90) reduce the increasingly negative gradient_drift_cosine without giving back Best; and is there any interval whose amplitude increase is absorbed by matching (assignment_switch_fraction) rather than converted into core-atom displacement. Maximum Best has been 7.7080 in every round versus teacher 7.8378, so Best potential remains an untested axis rather than a saturated one.",
